// A recursive generic that grows its binding at every step — f(some(x))
// instantiates f<?i32>, f<??i32>, ... — hits the instance cap instead of
// chaining until the global limit with a misleading message (Phase 2.4
// audit). Optionals grow the mangle by one char per step, so the 512-byte
// name buffer cannot fire before the 256-instance cap.
// EXPECT-ERROR: too many generic instances (max 256)
fn f<T>(x: T) {
    f(some(x))
}
f(5)
